every year the battle between Microsoft  and Apple gets more and more intense  this year let's see who came out on top  what's going on guys my name is David  homage and welcome back to the channel  if you're new here smash that subscribe  button and join us as we talk all things  tech today we're looking at the  Microsoft Surface laptop 3 and we're  looking at the 2019  MacBook Pro more specifically we're  going to be looking at the intro model  of both of these devices as they're the  best selling devices for each brand  let's start with some big-ticket items  the price the Microsoft Surface laptop 3  in Australia starts with 1357 or 933 USD  whilst the MacBook Pro starts from 1999  Australian or 1375 USD you can get 10%  off both of these devices if you're a  university student so that's definitely  something to keep in mind so the first  point for the price category goes to  Microsoft tech specs for the base  surface laptop 3 you get a 10th  generation eye 5 Intel Core chip 8  gigabytes of RAM and 128 gigabytes of  SSD storage whilst in the MacBook Pro  you get an eighth-generation eye 5 intel  core processor with also 8 gigabytes of  RAM and 128 gigabytes of SSD storage so  on paper when you're comparing these two  base level specs you find that the  Microsoft gains an additional point here  but when you stop looking at the paper  figures and you actually start looking  at the device you find that the ports  become a very big problem on the  Microsoft Surface laptop 3 you get a USB  a a USB C a headphone jack and also a  proprietary fast charging connector  whilst on the MacBook Pro you get four  USB C ports with two of those ports  being Thunderbolt 3 you don't get any  Thunderbolts on the Microsoft Surface  laptop 3 so if you look at these two  devices at the surface laptop 3 probably  more compatible ports for this day and  age you're not going to need any  adapters to use any of your old devices  or any of your new devices going forward  but in a couple years time you probably  will need to convert that single USB a  to a USB C to run all your latest tech  whilst Apple on the other hand has given  you advantage of going for all four USB  C ports this might not be a great  advantage to start because you may have  to grab a couple of adapters or  alternatively go out and buy all new  tech that's USB C compatible but in the  future you're definitely going to be  better off as we all know Apple has  always been the leaders in port  technology when it comes to tech a few  years ago you may remember that they  released the iPhone 7 with no headphone  jack this caused a lot of commotion and  everybody was up in arms however if you  think about it two years later every  single flagship device manufacturer  including Samsung themselves has quickly  removed all headphone jacks this is more  for a money kind of financial system  because they're able to create more  revenue from selling you their wireless  headphones then they were from selling  you some cheap cable headphones in the  past so if we look at this as an example  Apple going with the four USB C port on  the MacBook Pro definitely gives it the  advantage for future proofing and that's  why I'm giving the port's point to Apple  charging and battery life this is a  pretty big category in my opinion  charging is everything I don't really  like charged my devices overnight  especially if I know I need it a couple  hours later and also considering the  fact that laptops are meant to be a  travel device you really want your  devices to be long lasting and quick  charging the surface laptop three  charges from zero to 80% in under one  hour and has a theoretical runtime of  eleven and a half hours which you may or  may not have noticed is significantly  less than the surface laptop two which  had a theoretical runtime of fourteen  and a half hours I know I personally  experienced on my old surface laptop too  that you could get about 16 hours of  runtime off this device which is  significantly more than what  promising in the surfs laptop three  whilst the Apple MacBook Pro has a  theoretical charge time from zero to 80%  in under two hours and a total  theoretical battery runtime of 10.5  hours sorry Apple this is a very great  attempt but the point again goes to  Microsoft moving on to the screen  quality because for me screen quality is  very important you don't want to be  thinking I know I can't see my screen  it's too dark it's not clear it's blurry  especially when you're paying anywhere  between 1300 and 2000 straigh llion  dollars for a laptop this is where the  surface three starts to show some cracks  with 318 it's of brightness 201 pixels  per inch and a 10-point touchscreen  display you'd think this is pretty good  quality how about when you compare it to  the Apple MacBook Pro you find that it's  a very different story the MacBook Pro  has 500 nits of brightness 227 pixels  per inch but no touchscreen display it  does promise 25% more colors than the  srgb range that's inside the Microsoft  Surface laptop 3 and it does offer you  the true tone color display so if you've  ever used one of these Retina screens  you know for a fact that Apple screen is  significantly better than anything that  Microsoft's produced to date so we  currently stand at three points to  Microsoft and two points to Apple  keyboards and trackpads the Microsoft  Surface laptop - already had a fantastic  keyboard that was miles ahead of the  2018 MacBook Pro so when they brought  out the surface laptop 3 you knew they  were gonna make it better the surface  laptop 3s keyboard is just that little  bit quieter just that little bit nicer  and just that little bit better than  anything else on the market nonetheless  the MacBook Pro still does have a very  nice butterfly keyboard with ultra quiet  keys this isn't any disadvantage the  MacBook Pro but in my personal opinion  it isn't as nice to type it isn't as  easy to type and after a while you just  start to get annoyed because your  fingertips hurt because there's no  rebound on the  it's just like tapping aluminium all day  it is rumoured 2020 MacBook Pro will  solve this issue with a brand new  keyboard setup but until it's released  we don't know what Apple's gonna launch  looking at the two trackpads personally  for me they're both really really good I  don't find a fault in either of them  they're both a nice large size with the  MacBooks being slightly bigger and  slightly easy to use but when you  compare them like for like there isn't  too much of a difference in my opinion  so unfortunately for the poor quality of  the keyboard on the MacBook side things  I'm rewarding this point against a  Microsoft ecosystems and compatibility  Microsoft  well what ecosystem it doesn't really  have anything integrated between its  devices the MacBook Pro on the other  hand has this very user-friendly very  inviting Apple experience between its  devices if you have an iPhone and iPad  and a MacBook well your life just got a  hell of a lot easier  unfortunately for Apple it still does  have some compatibility issues when  programs are concerned you can run boot  camp and parallel on it to fix these  problems so that takes away from the con  entirely when we're talking ecosystems  Apple definitely gets the point I could  keep this comparison going on forever if  I'm being honest with you and at the end  of the day both devices would end up  neck-and-neck the surface laptop 3 and  2019 MacBook Pro are both incredible  pieces of tech with their own pros and  cons personally if I was to go out and  buy one of these devices today and only  use one of these devices well it would  be the Microsoft Surface laptop 3 for  the sole purpose of the better keyboard  if the new 20/20 MacBook Pro comes out  with a competitive keyboard that's just  as nice to use as a surface laptop 3 and  also comes it out with a competitive  price tag that isn't 700 Australian  dollars more than the surface laptop 3  then my personal opinion will change and  the crown will go to Apple but for the  time being I personally believe that the  surface laptop 3 comes out on top for  price compatibility and just the general  user experience that's all from me guys  thanks so much for watching if you  enjoyed the video make sure you smash  that subscribe button  20-19 style and as always I'll see you  next Monday

